    "sticky_notes": [
        {
            "id": "note_intro",
            "text": "**Lanes: Repeat** A lane is a variable-length array of floats. **Repeat** takes one scalar and copies it to N lanes, with optional spread to offset each lane.",
            "x": -220.0,
            "y": 50.0,
            "width": 300.0,
            "height": 120.0,
            "color": 0
        },
        {
            "id": "note_repeat",
            "text": "**Repeat (golden + random spread)** Both X and Y LFOs drive separate Repeat nodes, spreading 8 lanes in 2D. A slow sawtooth LFO drives the **rotation** param on both, smoothly cycling which ball gets which offset — creating a spinning effect.",
            "x": -220.0,
            "y": 200.0,
            "width": 300.0,
            "height": 120.0,
            "color": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "note_scalar",
            "text": "**Scalar auto-broadcast** The radius LFO connects as a scalar — it automatically applies to all 8 lanes. No Repeat needed for shared values.",
            "x": 90.0,
            "y": 200.0,
            "width": 260.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "note_modes",
            "text": "**Try the other modes!** Click the Repeat node and change mode:\n- **copy**: all identical\n- **random**: scattered offsets\n- **phase**: 0-1 ramp\n- **golden**: maximally decorrelated",
            "x": 90.0,
            "y": 330.0,
            "width": 260.0,
            "height": 130.0,
            "color": 2
        },
        {
            "id": "note_next",
